{"summary":{"text":"GoCardless (UK bank-payments fintech) reported FY24 (Jul2023-Jun2024) revenue growth and narrowing losses, then was acquired by Mollie in Sept 2026; standalone post-merger financials are not yet disclosed in these sources.","source_ids":["F3","F9"]},
"observations":[{"metric":"other","label":"Statement of capital after share allotment (GBP)","candidate_id":"N9","period":"P2","qualification":"reported","meaning":"Companies House filing shows nominal share capital of GBP 322,382,286 following a share allotment dated 27 Aug 2026; this reflects equity structure, not cash raised or valuation.","}
],
"findings":[{"text":"GoCardless's FY24 press release (period 1 Jul 2023-30 Jun 2024) states Group revenue of £126.8m (+38% YoY) and total income of £132.8m including interest income, with net losses falling 55% to £35.1m from £78.0m.","source_ids":["F3"]},{"text":"FY24 growth was broad-based: international revenue rose 47% to £30.8m and UK&Ireland revenue rose 35% to £96.0m, per the same company press release, alongside a completed Sentenial/Nuapay acquisition in Sept 2024.","source_ids":["F3"]},{"text":"The company reports £39.6bn in payments processed in FY24 (28% YoY) for over 94,000 organisations, a transaction-volume and customer-count claim distinct from revenue; separate marketing pages claim 'nearly 100,000', '100,000+' or '80,000+' businesses without consistent dates, so exact current customer counts are not independently verifiable.","source_ids":["F3","F6","F7","F8"]},{"text":"Mollie announced completion of its acquisition of GoCardless on 1 Sept 2026; the combined group claims over 350,000 businesses across 30+ markets and Pay by Bank availability across 38 countries, but this scope now includes Mollie's own business, not GoCardless alone.","source_ids":["F9"]}],
"outlook":[{"case":"downside","condition":"If GoCardless's standalone results are no longer separately disclosed after being folded into Mollie's group structure (new holding company registered Sept 2024, per Companies House).","implication":"Investors and observers could lose visibility into whether GoCardless's own revenue growth and loss reduction trend (seen in FY24) continued, masking any deterioration inside the combined entity.","watch":"Absence of GoCardless-specific segment disclosure in future Mollie group accounts or Companies House filings would confirm reduced transparency.","source_ids":["F2","F9"]},{"case":"base","condition":"If GoCardless continues the FY24 pattern of revenue growth and shrinking net losses without major integration disruption after the Mollie acquisition.","implication":"The declared 'clear path to profitability' cited by management for FY24 could continue toward an operating breakeven, though this remains a stated target, not an achieved result.","watch":"Future Companies House group accounts (e.g., the FY25 filing dated 12 Apr 2026 covering to 30 Jun 2025, once its figures are published) showing continued margin improvement would support this case.","source_ids":["F3","F1"]},{"case":"upside","condition":"If combining GoCardless's Pay by Bank network with Mollie's card/local-payment and financing products across a claimed 350,000+ combined business base drives incremental adoption.","implication":"Cross-selling could expand GoCardless's transaction volumes and international revenue mix faster than its FY24 standalone growth rates, though no post-merger financials are yet available to confirm this.","watch":"Reported combined-entity revenue, customer counts, or country coverage disclosed by Mollie/GoCardless in subsequent press releases or filings would indicate whether this materializes.","source_ids":["F9"]}],
"needs":[{"kind":"public_source","question":"Can the FY25 Companies House group accounts (filed 12 Apr 2026, covering to 30 June 2025) be retrieved for updated revenue and loss figures?","why":"Only FY24 (to Jun 2024) figures are narratively available here; FY25 accounts exist per the filing history but their content was not supplied."},{"kind":"identity","question":"Will GoCardless Ltd continue filing standalone UK accounts, or will results be consolidated only within Mollie/GoCardless Holdings (UK) Ltd going forward?","why":"A new UK holding company was registered in Sept 2024 and the Mollie acquisition completed in Sept 2026, changing the group's reporting entity and scope."}]}

